          "event loop and async I/O"
        ],
        [
          "Operating system",
          "pink",
          "files, network, processes"
        ]
      ],
      "say": "Node is built from a few pieces. Your code runs on V8, the same engine as Chrome, which compiles JavaScript to machine code. A library called libuv provides the event loop and asynchronous input and output, and talks to the operating system.",
      "voice": "/audio/node-01-what-is-node/engine.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "thread",
      "min": 9,
      "duration": 15.0,
      "text": "One thread, many connections.",
      "say": "Your JavaScript runs on a single main thread. Waiting for a file or a network response is handed off to the operating system, so one thread can serve thousands of connections. The catch: heavy computation on that thread blocks everything.",
